ess CPU/memory per request\n- Prevents connection exhaustion (OS limits open sockets)\n- Throughput scales under load—reusing beats making thousands of new connections\n\n**Without pooling:** Each request creates connection → authenticate → query → close. Handshake + auth = expensive. Under load = many sockets open = system buckles.\n\n**With pooling:** Create N connections once. Many requests cycle through them. Near-zero overhead per request.","ttft_ms":7708,"type":"result","duration_ms":8888,"uuid":"99f7fde9-0508-4d9f-b172-3d1f8a65f002","ttft_stream_ms":790,"time_to_request_ms":124,"first_content_frame_ms":790,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":10,"outputTokens":710,"cacheReadInputTokens":7864,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0043464,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":526,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-12T05:14:51.381Z"}